    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0136" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4677½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sato</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: Referring to our
                    conversation of this morning, in order to avoid any possible misunderstanding,
                    may I ask you to be good enough to give me a memorandum setting forth <pb
                        facs="0137" n="63" xml:id="pg63"/> the main points of your suggestion about
                    a Japanese mission to the United States as to the questions to be dealt with and
                    the composition of the mission. Am I right to understand that the commission
                    being “sentimental” as well as technical, is expected to discuss matters
                    pertaining to supplies to European Allies, naval cooperation, financing China,
                    as well as to exchange views on Far Eastern questions and possibly on the
                    so-called Japanese-American problem. Am I also right to understand that either
                    Root mission will visit Japan on its way home or a special mission will be sent
                    to my country.</p>
                <p>With high regard, I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aimaro Sato</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
